From e44fffc1b31f07dcefdd2177c7b3e12578ae0df6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:12:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] gateway: session.create/resume reply never waits on
 the banner inventory past 2 s
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Why: on the mini (Nov 13 02:44 PST) one canonical session.create took 84 s from ws accept to
reply against the client's 30 s RPC budget (hermes_cli/gateway_client.py DEFAULT_RPC_TIMEOUT).
AuthorityConnection.resume awaited snapshot_info -> session_inventory (every tool check_fn, the
xai credential pool ~7 s alone, the skills walk, MCP status, git, update check) under GIL load
before answering, so the client gave up and every retry paid the full cost again. The legacy
tui_gateway create already replied lazily; the authority path did not.

Fix (gateway/session_local_inventory.reply_info, used by resume and thus create):
- The reply waits at most REPLY_INVENTORY_BUDGET_S (2 s) for the inventory. Past it, the reply
  carries the lazy shape (tools {}, skills {}, mcp_servers [], inventory_pending: true) and the
  build keeps running; when it finishes the session publishes the full info as a session.info
  event (inventory_pending: false), merged with a fresh local_session_info so a turn started
  meanwhile is not reported idle.
- --oneshot / --source tool sessions (no banner, no status bar) skip the inventory entirely.
- Concurrent opens of one session (a second viewer, a client retry) share one in-flight build.
- session.info RPC (explicit ask) still returns the full inventory, unbounded.
- Contract: SessionInventoryFields.inventory_pending (regenerated TS/OpenRPC).
- Classic CLI: banner_inventory() returns None while inventory_pending, so it shows the compact
  banner instead of a full banner listing zero tools. Ink already renders "…" for lazy+empty and
  replaces info on session.info.

Proof:
- RED on base bc4eee92f1: test_create_reply_does_not_wait_on_a_60s_inventory_and_info_follows
  fails "session.create reply took 60.2s behind the inventory".
- GREEN: tests/gateway/test_session_create_inventory_budget.py (5 tests: 60 s inventory -> reply
  < 3 s and one late session.info; oneshot/tool never build; fast inventory rides the reply with no
  event; concurrent opens share one build) plus 53 files / 530 tests importing the touched modules
  and tests/hermes_cli/test_gateway_session_store.py (57) pass; scripts/check --base origin/main ok.
